Article 17

1. The Regional Government is responsible for the protection of the rights of Women and Children.
2. Responsibility as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: - 11 -a. education;
b. health;
c. politics;
d. law;
e. economy;
f. culture; andg. social.
3. The Regional Government's responsibility for the protection of Women's rights as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted by:  a. formulation of gender-responsive Regional policies;
b. institutionalization of gender mainstreaming within the Regional Government;
c. empowerment of Women in the political, legal, economic, cultural and social fields in community organizations at the regency level;
d. strengthening and development of service provider institutions for Women's empowerment at the regency level;
e. implementing Prevention efforts against Violence against Women.
4. The Regional Government's responsibility for the protection of Children's rights as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted by:a. formulation of policies, programs, and Regional development activities with a child rights perspective that are set forth in Regional development planning documents;
b. formulation of norms, standard procedures and assessment criteria for the fulfillment and protection of Children's rights that refer to norms, standards, procedures and criteria established by the government;
c. implementation of child-friendly regency shall be carried out in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
d. facilitation of the implementation of Regional Children's forum;
e. increasing Community participation in the implementation and protection of Children's rights;
f. monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of Children's fulfillment and Protection programs;
g. guidance of Child Protection institutions;
h. providing special protection for Children; andi. implementing Prevention efforts against Violence against Children.

Article 7

1. The form of Women's Protection services as referred to in Article 6 letter a includes:a. legal aid;
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation services;
d. complaint, consultation and counseling services;

e. social reintegration services; and
f. pre-marital guidance services.
2. Pre-marital guidance services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter f, shall be implemented by every Woman who will enter into marriage.
3. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be conducted to provide understanding and knowledge regarding family resilience, health, psychology, religion, social and culture.
4. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of Women's empowerment and Child Protection.
5. In implementing guidance as referred to in paragraph (4) the Regional Apparatus may involve: a. related agencies;
b. religious leaders; andc. traditional leaders.
6. Further provisions regarding the procedures for Women's Protection services shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

8 -

Article 21

1. The technical service institution as referred to in Article 20 paragraph (2) letter a shall be implemented by P2TP2A and FPK2PA.
2. In organizing the Protection of Women and Children, the Regional Government shall establish a regional technical implementing unit for Protection of Women and Children.
3. The establishment of the regional technical implementing unit as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be stipulated by Regent Regulation after obtaining written approval from the Governor.
4. In the case of implementing technical services as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may establish a task force.
(5) The task force as referred to in paragraph (4) may also carry out institutional strengthening through cooperation and coordination with: a. CFC task force;
b. CRA task force;
c. K/DRA task force;
d. schools and/or educational institutions;
e. Children's forum;
f. children's center;
g. community organizations;
h. Women's organizations; and i. other institutions concerned with the fulfillment of rights and Protection of Children.
6. The task force as referred to in paragraph (4) constitutes a coordinative institution at the district and sub-district level that coordinates policies, programs and activities to realize sub-districts, child-friendly villages/wards.
7. Further provisions regarding technical services as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

